\ End-to-end exercise of a `method{` dispatch on a user-defined virtual
\ type under runtime-image AOT. The dispatch entry is registered at
\ freeze time keyed on the virtual TypeValue's descriptor; the runtime
\ push of that TypeValue goes through the slot table.
\
\ User-side dispatch registrations do not yet replay across the
\ freeze->runtime boundary, so the generic body's fallthrough behavior
\ runs at runtime. The test exercises the build path and that
\ observable runtime behavior.

box: virtual{ fixnum } ;

bump: generic ( s -- n ) [ drop -1 ] ;
bump: method{ box } [ unmake-box 1 + ] ;

5 make-box bump .
9 >box bump .

\ Predicate still works through the slot table even without the user
\ method replaying.
5 make-box box? .
"not-a-box" box? .
